fnm env --use-on-cd --shell powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
fnm env --use-on-cd | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

First, define the icon parts in the icons$1 function:
// In the icons$1 function
icn["TP.YOUR_NEW_POINT"] = [
    // Basic shape/path
    {
        type: "path",  // Can be "path", "circle", "text" etc.
        d: "M 100,100 L...",  // SVG path data
        fill: false,  // or fillColor for filled shapes
    },
    // Additional elements
    {
        type: "text",
        alignmentBaseline: "middle",
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "middle",
        x: 100,
        y: 140,
        fontsize: 40,
        text: "YourText"
    }
];

Define the label positions in the tacticalPoints function:

// In the tacticalPoints function
sidc["YOUR_SIDC"] = {
    additionalInformation: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "middle",
        x: 100,
        y: -70,
        fontsize: 40
    },
    hostile: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "start",
        x: 150,
        y: 45,
        fontsize: 40
    },
    uniqueDesignation: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "start",
        x: 150,
        y: -30,
        fontsize: 40
    },
    dtg: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "end",
        x: 50,
        y: -30,
        fontsize: 40
    }
};

3. Map the SIDC to the icon and define its bounding box in the tacticalpoints object:

// In the tacticalpoints.icons function
if (symbolSet == "25") {  // For tactical points
    sidc["YOUR_SIDC"] = icn["TP.YOUR_NEW_POINT"];
    bbox["YOUR_SIDC"] = {
        x1: 60,  // Left boundary
        x2: 140, // Right boundary
        y1: -60, // Top boundary
        y2: 140  // Bottom boundary
    };
}

Example of adding a new tactical point:
// 1. Define the icon parts
icn["TP.NEW_CHECKPOINT"] = [
    // Base circle
    {
        type: "circle",
        fill: false,
        cx: 100,
        cy: 100,
        r: 40
    },
    // Cross lines
    {
        type: "path",
        d: "M 80,100 L 120,100 M 100,80 L 100,120",
        fill: false
    },
    // Label
    {
        type: "text",
        alignmentBaseline: "middle",
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "middle",
        x: 100,
        y: 140,
        fontsize: 40,
        text: "CP"
    }
];

// 2. Define label positions
sidc["240100"] = {  // Your SIDC
    additionalInformation: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "middle",
        x: 100,
        y: -70,
        fontsize: 40
    },
    uniqueDesignation: {
        stroke: false,
        textanchor: "start",
        x: 150,
        y: -30,
        fontsize: 40
    }
};

// 3. Map SIDC to icon
if (symbolSet == "25") {
    sidc["240100"] = icn["TP.NEW_CHECKPOINT"];
    bbox["240100"] = { x1: 60, x2: 140, y1: -60, y2: 140 };
}
Key points to remember:
Icons are built using SVG elements (paths, circles, text)
Label positions are defined separately for flexibility
Each symbol needs a unique SIDC mapping
Bounding boxes help with symbol placement
Follow the naming convention "TP." for tactical points
Use the existing patterns for consistency (like actionPoint for common layouts)



